WEBVTT

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.291
We're here.

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.445
The glacial fractures
are stable.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.749
We're clear to beam inside.

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.655
Acknowledged.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.470
Not exactly the way
I remember it.

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:28.393
Power grid's been destroyed.

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:32.734
Neural gel packs... frozen solid.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:36.434
Decks 9 through 14
are now Deck 10.

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:37.874
They've been compacted.

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:40.174
Looks like they hit the ice
at full impulse.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.505
The EMH?

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:45.050
I'm trying to access Sick Bay.

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.608
The relays aren't responding.

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:47.948
I'm losing the interface.

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:49.113
Reset the power cell.

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:55.820
Come on!

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:57.055
Let's get moving.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.722
Keep an open com-link.

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:32.718
Chakotay to Tessa.

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:33.850
Go ahead.

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:35.416
I found her.

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:37.827
Lock on to the transporter relay
and beam her to the lab.

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:38.829
Stand by.

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.160
Make it quick.

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:43.828
This isn't exactly
a happy reunion.

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:45.564
I've got a lock.

00:06:52.879 --> 00:06:54.346
Please state the nature of...

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.403
Long time no see.

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:56.413
Ensign.

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:57.414
I go by Harry now.

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:58.415
It's a long story.

00:06:58.484 --> 00:06:59.951
Where's your mobile emitter?

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.883
What's happened to the ship?
The crew?

00:07:01.988 --> 00:07:03.080
No time. The emitter.

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:04.384
It's in here, but...

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:07.887
Here.

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:09.289
Slap it on and let's go.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:11.592
Wait. I demand an explanation.

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:14.360
I'll give you one.

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:16.925
We're here to change history.

00:07:53.339 --> 00:07:57.537
Ladies and gentlemen, please...

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:58.838
may I introduce

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:02.642
the next generation
of instellar propulsion...

00:08:02.715 --> 00:08:06.651
the quantum slipstream drive.

00:08:08.721 --> 00:08:12.555
Four years, two months,
11 days...

00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:14.616
that's precisely how long

00:08:14.694 --> 00:08:17.219
Voyager's been
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:08:17.296 --> 00:08:18.729
And during that time,

00:08:18.798 --> 00:08:21.733
we've advanced
the frontiers of exploration

00:08:21.801 --> 00:08:24.167
and, more importantly,
we've survived.

00:08:24.237 --> 00:08:25.761
Hear, hear.

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:27.738
Now it's time to go home.

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:31.434
Enjoy the celebration,
but keep in mind,

00:08:31.511 --> 00:08:34.275
we've still got a lot of work
to do before tomorrow's flight.

00:08:34.347 --> 00:08:36.247
Go easy on that champagne,
Lieutenant.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.417
Quantum matrix...

00:08:39.485 --> 00:08:40.645
Benamite crystals...

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:41.914
Borg technology...

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:44.046
Can you imagine
what Starfleet is going to say?

00:08:44.123 --> 00:08:45.715
I don't think
we'll hear any complaints.

00:08:45.791 --> 00:08:47.554
The Federation's
first slipstream drive...

00:08:47.627 --> 00:08:49.754
they'll probably nominate us
for the Cochrane Medal of Honor.

00:08:49.829 --> 00:08:51.660
I'll start working
on my acceptance speech.

00:08:51.731 --> 00:08:53.596
"I'd like to thank
the Borg collective..."

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:54.598
Dinner plans?

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:56.259
Nothing special.
Date with a replicator.

00:08:56.335 --> 00:08:57.302
Cancel it.
That's an order.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:58.860
Aye, Captain.

00:08:59.906 --> 00:09:01.066
Lieutenant?

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.402
Lieutenant.

00:09:02.475 --> 00:09:04.136
Excuse me.

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:07.577
My contribution
to the slipstream drive.

00:09:07.647 --> 00:09:09.171
Thanks.
What is it?

00:09:09.248 --> 00:09:11.876
A Talaxian furfly.

00:09:12.018 --> 00:09:15.283
An old spacefaring tradition
among my people.

00:09:15.354 --> 00:09:17.879
If one of these creatures
stowed away on your ship,

00:09:17.957 --> 00:09:20.357
it was a sign of good fortune.

00:09:20.426 --> 00:09:22.417
I had this little fellow
preserved.

00:09:22.495 --> 00:09:25.123
He hung in my engine room
for six years.

00:09:26.699 --> 00:09:28.064
Cute.

00:09:28.134 --> 00:09:31.501
Mr. Neelix, you are an unending
source of astonishment.

00:09:31.571 --> 00:09:32.936
Why, thank you, Mr. Vulcan.

00:09:42.615 --> 00:09:44.310
Seven?

00:09:44.383 --> 00:09:47.875
My visual processors
and motor cortex...

00:09:47.954 --> 00:09:50.388
they are malfunctioning.

00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:53.323
Sounds like a problem
with your cortical implant.

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:54.518
We'd better have a look.

00:09:56.362 --> 00:09:57.488
Hold still.

00:09:57.563 --> 00:09:59.394
I cannot comply.

00:09:59.465 --> 00:10:01.023
You're intoxicated.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:02.397
Impossible.

00:10:02.468 --> 00:10:05.130
Your blood synthehol level
is.05 percent.

00:10:05.204 --> 00:10:07.434
How many glasses of champagne
did you consume?

00:10:07.506 --> 00:10:08.734
One.

00:10:08.808 --> 00:10:10.799
Obviously, the Borg
can't hold their liquor.

00:10:10.876 --> 00:10:11.934
Come to Sick Bay.

00:10:12.044 --> 00:10:13.944
I'll give you some inaprovaline
to counteract the effects.

00:10:14.046 --> 00:10:16.412
I was simply trying
to perfect my social skills

00:10:16.482 --> 00:10:17.915
as you instructed me to do.

00:10:17.984 --> 00:10:19.383
And you're doing a fine job.

00:10:21.654 --> 00:10:22.621
You have always been

00:10:22.688 --> 00:10:24.485
of enormous assistance
to me, Doctor.

00:10:24.557 --> 00:10:26.821
You... you are my mentor.

00:10:26.892 --> 00:10:28.154
Yes.

00:10:28.227 --> 00:10:31.685
We are as one.
We are as one.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.131
Did you see that?

00:10:36.202 --> 00:10:37.294
Hmm.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:40.931
I think our drone did
a little too much celebrating.

00:10:41.007 --> 00:10:42.975
Speaking of which, when are
you going to join the party?

00:10:43.075 --> 00:10:45.066
In a minute.

00:10:45.144 --> 00:10:48.477
You're running a warp core
diagnostic now?

00:10:48.547 --> 00:10:52.643
Harry, I think
we built an Edsel.

00:10:52.718 --> 00:10:53.810
A what?

00:10:53.886 --> 00:10:56.980
A lemon;
a disaster waiting to happen.

00:10:57.123 --> 00:11:00.456
I ran a simulation last night

00:11:00.526 --> 00:11:02.926
and I discovered
a.42 phase variance

00:11:03.062 --> 00:11:04.927
in the slipstream threshold.

00:11:05.064 --> 00:11:07.931
.42?
So it'll be a bumpy ride.

00:11:08.067 --> 00:11:09.091
We've flown through worse.

00:11:09.168 --> 00:11:10.567
If we get knocked out of
that slipstream mid-flight...

00:11:11.904 --> 00:11:14.464
it could overload
the quantum matrix.

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:15.939
Did you tell the Captain?

00:11:16.008 --> 00:11:17.305
Not yet.

00:11:17.376 --> 00:11:19.276
I didn't want to spoil
the festivities

00:11:19.345 --> 00:11:20.403
until I was sure.

00:11:20.479 --> 00:11:22.913
Tom, if it'll make you
feel better,

00:11:22.982 --> 00:11:24.609
we'll go
to the holodeck right now,

00:11:24.684 --> 00:11:26.151
run a few more simulations.

00:11:26.218 --> 00:11:27.708
It's probably
just a sensor glitch.

00:11:28.754 --> 00:11:30.745
We're at full impulse.

00:11:30.823 --> 00:11:33.053
Engaging slipstream drive.

00:11:33.125 --> 00:11:35.286
Quantum field is stable.

00:11:35.361 --> 00:11:37.261
Deflector at maximum.

00:11:37.329 --> 00:11:42.665
Slipstream velocity
in four, three, two...

00:11:46.072 --> 00:11:47.232
Power output is steady.

00:11:47.306 --> 00:11:49.740
Quantum field is holding.

00:11:49.809 --> 00:11:52.175
Shields down to 73 percent.

00:11:52.244 --> 00:11:53.438
Looking good.

00:11:53.512 --> 00:11:55.139
Keep that deflector aligned
and we should be...

00:11:57.249 --> 00:11:59.240
We've got a phase variance...
point one.

00:11:59.318 --> 00:12:00.512
Point two.

00:12:00.586 --> 00:12:02.520
Remodulate the deflector.

00:12:02.588 --> 00:12:04.385
No effect.
Point four.

00:12:04.457 --> 00:12:05.890
I'm shutting down the drive.

00:12:05.958 --> 00:12:07.619
No, wait. I want to invert
the quantum field.

00:12:07.693 --> 00:12:08.921
It's no use.

00:12:08.994 --> 00:12:10.962
That slipstream is collapsing.

00:12:12.998 --> 00:12:15.364
Inertial dampers are off-line.

00:12:15.434 --> 00:12:16.901
Warning.
Hull breach on Deck 10.

00:12:16.969 --> 00:12:18.527
We're losing
structural integrity.

00:12:18.604 --> 00:12:20.572
Computer, freeze program!

00:12:23.175 --> 00:12:24.870
One more time.
I think if we reroute

00:12:24.944 --> 00:12:26.741
emergency power to the deflector
a little earlier...

00:12:26.812 --> 00:12:27.870
It won't help.

00:12:27.947 --> 00:12:28.914
Computer,

00:12:28.981 --> 00:12:30.642
restart simulation
at time index...

00:12:30.716 --> 00:12:32.115
Computer, belay that order.

00:12:32.184 --> 00:12:33.481
It's no use, Harry.

00:12:33.552 --> 00:12:34.712
We can't just give up.

00:12:34.787 --> 00:12:37.187
23 simulations, 23 catastrophes.

00:12:37.256 --> 00:12:39.156
This is no sensor glitch.

00:12:42.695 --> 00:12:44.322
We've got to tell them.

00:12:44.396 --> 00:12:45.590
That can't be right.

00:12:45.664 --> 00:12:48.292
We tested this engine
molecule by molecule.

00:12:48.367 --> 00:12:49.800
I'm sorry, B'Elanna.

00:12:49.869 --> 00:12:52.167
I wish to examine
the results of the simulation.

00:12:52.238 --> 00:12:53.967
Holodeck 2...
run them for yourself.

00:12:54.106 --> 00:12:56.973
That is, if you don't mind being
vaporized a few dozen times.

00:12:57.109 --> 00:12:58.838
I looked at their findings,
Captain.

00:12:58.911 --> 00:13:01.004
If we try to take
that flight in the morning,

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:02.877
we'll be in escape pods
by afternoon.

00:13:02.948 --> 00:13:05.610
It would appear we have
no choice but to cancel it.

00:13:05.684 --> 00:13:09.142
Either that or...

00:13:09.221 --> 00:13:11.052
we can try it Harry's way.

00:13:11.123 --> 00:13:13.091
Ensign?

00:13:16.595 --> 00:13:17.619
I've got an idea.

00:13:17.696 --> 00:13:19.823
It's tricky,
but I think it could work.

00:13:19.899 --> 00:13:22.766
The trouble begins about
17 seconds into the flight.

00:13:22.835 --> 00:13:24.462
The phase variance kicks in

00:13:24.537 --> 00:13:26.402
and the slipstream
becomes unstable.

00:13:26.472 --> 00:13:28.440
What we need is
someone in a shuttle

00:13:28.507 --> 00:13:30.668
to ride the rapids
in front of Voyager.

00:13:30.743 --> 00:13:31.903
Yes.

00:13:31.977 --> 00:13:34.377
They could map the threshold
of the slipstream

00:13:34.446 --> 00:13:35.538
as it's forming

00:13:35.614 --> 00:13:37.741
and send the phase corrections
back to us.

00:13:37.817 --> 00:13:39.580
That is a great idea, Harry.

00:13:39.652 --> 00:13:42.450
Now, here's the tricky part.

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:45.589
The shuttle will only be

00:13:45.658 --> 00:13:47.785
a couple of seconds
ahead of Voyager.

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:49.521
That doesn't give
auto-navigation

00:13:49.595 --> 00:13:50.857
much time to compensate.

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.091
Tom?

00:13:53.165 --> 00:13:54.792
Couple of seconds?

00:13:54.867 --> 00:13:56.334
We can do this, Captain.

00:13:56.402 --> 00:13:57.664
Put me on that shuttle.

00:13:57.736 --> 00:14:00.034
I'll get Voyager
through the slipstream.

00:14:03.709 --> 00:14:05.267
What choice do we have?

00:14:05.344 --> 00:14:06.606
Take the drive off-line?

00:14:06.679 --> 00:14:08.169
Months of work for nothing?

00:14:08.247 --> 00:14:10.477
We built a highly experimental
piece of technology.

00:14:10.549 --> 00:14:11.914
There were bound to be setbacks.

00:14:12.051 --> 00:14:14.383
The benamite crystals
at the heart of this engine

00:14:14.453 --> 00:14:15.920
have already started to decay.

00:14:15.988 --> 00:14:19.321
It could take years
to synthesize more.

00:14:19.391 --> 00:14:22.326
I don't know
about the rest of you,

00:14:22.394 --> 00:14:24.089
but I didn't do all this work

00:14:24.163 --> 00:14:28.156
just to be stopped
by a.42 phase variance.

00:14:28.234 --> 00:14:29.701
No offense, Captain.

00:14:29.768 --> 00:14:32.032
None taken.

00:14:32.104 --> 00:14:34.402
All right, Mr. Kim...

00:14:34.473 --> 00:14:36.703
you've convinced me.

00:14:36.775 --> 00:14:38.037
Prepare a flight plan

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:40.544
and have it on my desk
within the hour.

00:14:40.613 --> 00:14:42.376
Yes, ma'am.

00:14:42.448 --> 00:14:44.643
I'll let you know what I decide.

00:14:54.526 --> 00:14:55.550
Come in.

00:14:57.496 --> 00:15:00.329
Commander, I hope
you've got an appetite.

00:15:00.399 --> 00:15:02.424
Famished, but I assumed
you called me here

00:15:02.501 --> 00:15:04.230
to talk about
the slipstream flight.

00:15:04.303 --> 00:15:06.601
No reason to cancel
our dinner plans.

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:09.332
I've programmed a dish

00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:11.569
my grandmother used
to make back on Earth...

00:15:11.644 --> 00:15:13.441
vegetable biryani.

00:15:13.512 --> 00:15:15.139
Sounds delicious.

00:15:15.214 --> 00:15:16.647
I didn't know you could cook.

00:15:16.715 --> 00:15:19.843
Normally, I draw the line
at a pot of coffee,

00:15:19.919 --> 00:15:21.853
but tonight
is a special occasion.

00:15:21.921 --> 00:15:23.855
Oh?

00:15:23.923 --> 00:15:25.914
Our last night
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:15:26.025 --> 00:15:27.754
I'd say that's special enough.

00:15:28.827 --> 00:15:31.455
You've made your decision.

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:33.555
We launch tomorrow at 0800.

00:15:33.632 --> 00:15:35.623
You and Harry
will take the Delta Flyer.

00:15:35.701 --> 00:15:37.430
Voyager will be
right behind you.

00:15:40.339 --> 00:15:42.500
The crew will be pleased.

00:15:42.574 --> 00:15:44.371
You can give them
the news yourself...

00:15:44.443 --> 00:15:46.411
after dessert.

00:15:49.615 --> 00:15:51.048
What about you, Chakotay?

00:15:51.116 --> 00:15:52.947
What do you think
about my decision?

00:15:57.022 --> 00:15:59.456
I've analyzed
Harry's flight plan.

00:15:59.525 --> 00:16:01.186
The theory is sound,

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:02.887
but there are just
too many variables.

00:16:03.028 --> 00:16:05.121
If something goes wrong
in that slipstream...

00:16:05.197 --> 00:16:07.597
This could be our only chance
to use the quantum drive.

00:16:07.666 --> 00:16:10.294
True, but if you
showed this data

00:16:10.369 --> 00:16:12.428
to any Starfleet engineer,

00:16:12.504 --> 00:16:15.598
they'd think we were
out of our minds.

00:16:15.674 --> 00:16:17.232
We can find another way home.

00:16:17.309 --> 00:16:18.537
We've waited this long.

00:16:18.610 --> 00:16:20.601
Long enough.
We've waited long enough.

00:16:23.382 --> 00:16:26.283
I know it's a risk...

00:16:26.352 --> 00:16:29.446
probably our biggest one yet...

00:16:29.521 --> 00:16:31.113
but I'm willing to take it.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:32.452
Are you with me?

00:16:32.524 --> 00:16:35.015
Always.

00:16:40.265 --> 00:16:42.233
Speaking of risks...

00:16:44.636 --> 00:16:47.537
are you ready to try
some home cooking?

00:16:47.606 --> 00:16:49.574
I'll alert Sick Bay.

00:17:09.828 --> 00:17:11.193
15 years?

00:17:11.263 --> 00:17:12.890
Give or take a few weeks.

00:17:13.032 --> 00:17:14.021
Where are we?

00:17:14.099 --> 00:17:16.897
In the Takara sector
just outside the Alpha Quadrant.

00:17:16.969 --> 00:17:17.901
The crew?

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:19.164
Except for us... dead.

00:17:19.238 --> 00:17:20.569
We think Captain Janeway

00:17:20.639 --> 00:17:23.437
tried to make an emergency
landing on this planet.

00:17:23.509 --> 00:17:25.909
The ship must have been
too heavily damaged.

00:17:26.045 --> 00:17:27.842
They were all killed on impact.

00:17:27.913 --> 00:17:29.710
You've been buried
inside a glacier

00:17:29.782 --> 00:17:31.215
for the past 15 years.

00:17:31.283 --> 00:17:35.276
You two were here,
on the Delta Flyer

00:17:35.354 --> 00:17:36.787
ahead of Voyager.

00:17:36.855 --> 00:17:38.288
You made it.

00:17:38.357 --> 00:17:39.915
All the way back to Earth.

00:17:40.025 --> 00:17:41.458
We got home, Doc,

00:17:41.527 --> 00:17:44.690
and all it took was killing
everyone we cared about.

00:17:44.763 --> 00:17:45.627
Harry.

00:17:46.965 --> 00:17:49.399
Starfleet certainly took
their time finding us.

00:17:49.468 --> 00:17:51.368
Starfleet...

00:17:51.437 --> 00:17:55.168
Starfleet gave up their search
for Voyager over nine years ago.

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:57.299
We had to find you on our own.

00:17:57.376 --> 00:18:01.870
Well, I don't know what
to say except... thank you.

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:05.245
I suppose I'd have stayed
in that deep freeze forever.

00:18:05.317 --> 00:18:07.251
We're not here
to salvage your program.

00:18:07.319 --> 00:18:10.152
We're here to prevent this
disaster from ever happening.

00:18:10.222 --> 00:18:12.156
You see, Doc,

00:18:12.224 --> 00:18:15.387
15 years ago, I miscalculated
the slipstream threshold

00:18:15.461 --> 00:18:18.726
and transmitted the wrong phase
corrections to Voyager.

00:18:18.797 --> 00:18:20.230
Boom.

00:18:20.299 --> 00:18:22.358
They were knocked
out of the slipstream

00:18:22.434 --> 00:18:23.833
and sent to an icy death.

00:18:23.902 --> 00:18:25.267
"Thank you, Ensign Kim."

00:18:25.337 --> 00:18:27.897
But I've had a long time
to rethink my mistake,

00:18:28.006 --> 00:18:31.237
and now I know how to fix it.

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:35.178
So... we're going
to send Voyager

00:18:35.247 --> 00:18:37.613
a new set of phase corrections.

00:18:39.251 --> 00:18:41.776
Isn't it a little late for that?

00:18:41.854 --> 00:18:44.516
We've found a way to communicate
with Voyager in the past,

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:45.750
just before the accident.

00:18:45.824 --> 00:18:47.086
Better late than never.

00:18:47.159 --> 00:18:49.457
A message back through time?

00:18:49.528 --> 00:18:50.517
Exactly.

00:18:50.596 --> 00:18:51.528
How?

00:18:58.871 --> 00:19:00.236
I don't understand.

00:19:00.305 --> 00:19:02.967
One of her cranial implants
is a transceiver

00:19:03.041 --> 00:19:04.406
designed to communicate
with other drones.

00:19:04.476 --> 00:19:05.408
That's right.

00:19:05.477 --> 00:19:07.536
It's called
an interplexing beacon.

00:19:07.613 --> 00:19:09.046
We want you
to extract the beacon

00:19:09.114 --> 00:19:10.843
and determine
its translink frequency.

00:19:10.916 --> 00:19:12.315
That shouldn't be a problem.

00:19:12.384 --> 00:19:14.284
She looks reasonably
well-preserved.

00:19:14.353 --> 00:19:17.015
Good. That'll tell us
where to send the message.

00:19:17.089 --> 00:19:20.058
Now, the hard part...
we need to know when to send it.

00:19:20.125 --> 00:19:22.616
Can you access
Seven's chronometric node

00:19:22.694 --> 00:19:25.356
and pinpoint the exact moment
her cybernetic implants

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:27.762
disengaged
from her organic systems?

00:19:27.833 --> 00:19:29.164
Her time of death?

00:19:29.234 --> 00:19:30.895
Down to the millisecond,
if possible.

00:19:31.036 --> 00:19:32.560
I'll see what I can do.

00:19:32.638 --> 00:19:34.606
I told you he'd come in handy.

00:19:36.441 --> 00:19:37.533
You said you'd found a way

00:19:37.609 --> 00:19:39.270
to communicate
with Seven in the past.

00:19:39.344 --> 00:19:40.311
How?

00:19:43.815 --> 00:19:47.216
Behold...
Salvage Component 36698...

00:19:47.286 --> 00:19:49.914
a Borg temporal transmitter.

00:19:50.055 --> 00:19:52.319
Starfleet Intelligence found it

00:19:52.391 --> 00:19:54.757
in the wreckage of a Borg cube
in the Beta Quadrant.

00:19:54.826 --> 00:19:55.918
We stole it.

00:19:59.631 --> 00:20:00.723
Trouble.

00:20:00.799 --> 00:20:03.131
Long-range sensors are picking
up a Federation vessel.

00:20:03.202 --> 00:20:04.260
How much time do we have?

00:20:04.336 --> 00:20:06.429
I entered a low orbit
and remodulated our shields,

00:20:06.505 --> 00:20:08.598
but it won't be long
before they find us.

00:20:08.674 --> 00:20:10.039
Six hours if we're lucky.

00:20:10.108 --> 00:20:11.735
Let me get this straight...

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:13.744
you're fugitives?

00:20:13.812 --> 00:20:15.643
"Galaxy's Most Wanted."

00:20:15.714 --> 00:20:17.909
We stole the Delta Flyer, too...

00:20:17.983 --> 00:20:19.951
right out
of a Federation shipyard.

00:20:20.085 --> 00:20:22.076
We're wanted on two counts
of high treason

00:20:22.154 --> 00:20:25.180
and conspiracy to violate
the Temporal Prime Directive.

00:20:25.257 --> 00:20:26.724
Wonderful.

00:20:26.792 --> 00:20:28.657
Out of the icebox
and into the fire.

00:20:28.727 --> 00:20:30.661
We don't have time for this.
Get started.

00:20:30.729 --> 00:20:32.287
Aye, sir.

00:20:32.364 --> 00:20:33.626
We still have to retrieve
those sensor logs.

00:20:33.699 --> 00:20:34.666
Get ready.

00:20:40.205 --> 00:20:41.331
Hello, Doctor.

00:20:41.406 --> 00:20:42.464
Do I know you?

00:20:42.541 --> 00:20:44.941
No, but I feel
like we're old friends.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:45.977
Tessa Omond.

00:20:46.044 --> 00:20:47.511
Hello.

00:20:47.579 --> 00:20:50.844
It's an honor to finally meet
Voyager's infamous EMH.

00:20:50.916 --> 00:20:52.440
"Infamous"?

00:20:52.517 --> 00:20:54.109
I've told her
a few horror stories.

00:20:54.186 --> 00:20:57.781
Actually, they've always
spoken very highly of you.

00:20:57.856 --> 00:20:59.790
Uh-huh... and how did
you get involved

00:20:59.858 --> 00:21:01.291
with Bonnie and Clyde here?

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:04.295
Oh, I've had an interest
in Voyager for a long time.

00:21:04.363 --> 00:21:05.796
They're having sex.

00:21:05.864 --> 00:21:07.525
Pardon?

00:21:07.599 --> 00:21:09.533
Chakotay and Tess.

00:21:09.601 --> 00:21:11.796
They're a couple;
joined at the hip.

00:21:13.171 --> 00:21:14.638
The truth is, Doctor,

00:21:14.706 --> 00:21:17.607
I didn't want Chakotay or Harry
to have to face this alone.

00:21:17.676 --> 00:21:18.904
I thought I could help.

00:21:21.346 --> 00:21:22.335
Ready?

00:21:22.414 --> 00:21:23.438
Stay warm.

00:21:35.727 --> 00:21:37.922
These controls
are a little clumsy.

00:21:37.996 --> 00:21:40.897
I thought you said this ship
was state of the art.

00:21:40.966 --> 00:21:42.160
It was at the time.

00:21:42.234 --> 00:21:44.395
I've located the sensor logs,

00:21:44.469 --> 00:21:48.098
but... the computer
is denying me access.

00:21:51.009 --> 00:21:54.035
My command codes should
still carry some weight.

00:22:03.822 --> 00:22:07.781
Hmm... looks like there's
an active file here.

00:22:08.994 --> 00:22:11.929
...but should our luck run out,
I'd like to say for the record

00:22:11.997 --> 00:22:14.465
that the crew of Voyager acted
with distinction and valor.

00:22:18.804 --> 00:22:20.738
You okay?

00:22:22.407 --> 00:22:24.068
Yes.

00:22:26.378 --> 00:22:28.642
It's just...

00:22:28.714 --> 00:22:31.512
the last time
I was in this chair,

00:22:31.583 --> 00:22:33.710
they were all here...

00:22:33.785 --> 00:22:35.616
alive.

00:22:39.124 --> 00:22:41.251
We're here to get them back.

00:22:45.197 --> 00:22:46.960
Can I see that tricorder?

00:22:59.544 --> 00:23:01.011
It's downloading.

00:23:01.079 --> 00:23:02.910
Give it a minute.

00:23:07.853 --> 00:23:10.378
I don't supposed we have time
for a tour?

00:23:10.455 --> 00:23:12.389
Afraid not.

00:23:12.457 --> 00:23:17.190
Besides,
I left my quarters a mess.

00:23:19.865 --> 00:23:24.097
In just a few hours,
if all goes as planned,

00:23:24.169 --> 00:23:26.501
we'll have changed history.

00:23:26.571 --> 00:23:30.098
The past 15 years... erased.

00:23:30.175 --> 00:23:32.575
We don't have to do this.

00:23:32.644 --> 00:23:34.737
Now you tell me.

00:23:34.813 --> 00:23:37.111
I'm serious.

00:23:37.182 --> 00:23:41.346
So am I, and I have
no intentions of backing out.

00:23:47.426 --> 00:23:49.053
Chakotay...

00:23:51.496 --> 00:23:53.964
Look at me...

00:23:54.065 --> 00:23:56.966
last minute jitters,
cold feet...

00:23:57.102 --> 00:23:59.434
I don't know what to call it.

00:23:59.504 --> 00:24:00.937
Ridiculous, isn't it?

00:24:01.006 --> 00:24:04.169
After all these years,
working toward this moment

00:24:04.242 --> 00:24:08.076
and when it finally comes,

00:24:08.146 --> 00:24:11.547
all I can think about
is losing you.

00:24:11.616 --> 00:24:15.177
Your heart has always
been here, on Voyager.

00:24:15.253 --> 00:24:17.346
That'll never change.

00:24:17.422 --> 00:24:19.982
This is where you belong.

00:24:22.260 --> 00:24:24.023
And who knows?

00:24:24.095 --> 00:24:26.529
Maybe we'll meet someday.

00:24:26.598 --> 00:24:29.761
But if we don't?

00:24:29.835 --> 00:24:32.360
Then I'll miss you all the same.

00:24:37.943 --> 00:24:39.934
...means all of that
has changed.

00:24:40.045 --> 00:24:42.138
You owe me one.

00:24:42.214 --> 00:24:44.944
Mr. Kim, your assistance,
please.

00:24:45.016 --> 00:24:46.677
Got to go.

00:24:51.890 --> 00:24:53.517
What was that all about?

00:24:53.592 --> 00:24:54.616
Oh, nothing.

00:24:54.693 --> 00:24:55.887
Letter to a friend.

00:24:55.961 --> 00:24:57.053
How does it look?

00:24:57.128 --> 00:24:58.925
No damage to the infrastructure,

00:24:58.997 --> 00:25:00.828
but I'll need an isoprobe.

00:25:00.899 --> 00:25:03.163
Way ahead of you, Doc.

00:25:08.406 --> 00:25:12.069
So, what was it like,
your homecoming?

00:25:12.143 --> 00:25:16.671
Antimatter fireworks,
longwinded dignitaries,

00:25:16.748 --> 00:25:18.682
a Vulcan children's choir.

00:25:18.750 --> 00:25:21.548
Oh, we got medals
pinned to our tunics.

00:25:21.620 --> 00:25:24.851
Chakotay gave a speech
commemorating the Voyager crew.

00:25:24.923 --> 00:25:26.857
Brought a tear
to everyone's eye.

00:25:26.925 --> 00:25:30.190
Admiral Maclntyre even wanted me
to marry his daughter.

00:25:30.262 --> 00:25:34.494
At least you weren't buried
under 20 meters of ice.

00:25:36.234 --> 00:25:39.795
You don't know how many times
I wished I was.

00:25:41.640 --> 00:25:44.165
I suppose
it must have been difficult

00:25:44.242 --> 00:25:49.202
with all your friends
and colleagues left behind.

00:25:51.883 --> 00:25:53.748
"Survivor guilt."

00:25:53.818 --> 00:25:55.786
Yeah. I heard a lot about that

00:25:55.854 --> 00:25:58.288
from the counselors
back at Headquarters.

00:25:58.356 --> 00:26:02.190
"You must learn to accept
the fact that you lived.

00:26:02.260 --> 00:26:04.251
"Embrace life.

00:26:04.329 --> 00:26:06.354
Move forward."

00:26:06.431 --> 00:26:09.457
I signed on to the first
deep space vessel

00:26:09.534 --> 00:26:11.001
I could find.

00:26:11.069 --> 00:26:12.900
We tried to calculate
where Voyager

00:26:13.038 --> 00:26:15.438
might have fallen
out of the slipstream.

00:26:15.507 --> 00:26:17.236
Four years of searching.

00:26:17.309 --> 00:26:18.708
We were close.

00:26:18.777 --> 00:26:20.210
I could feel it.

00:26:20.278 --> 00:26:22.803
Then, Starfleet Command
said it was time

00:26:22.881 --> 00:26:23.905
to end the search.

00:26:24.049 --> 00:26:26.779
"Low probability of success."

00:26:26.851 --> 00:26:30.378
All those admirals who shook
my hand at the homecoming...

00:26:30.455 --> 00:26:33.356
I went to see
every last one of them...

00:26:33.425 --> 00:26:36.553
begged them
to keep the search alive.

00:26:36.628 --> 00:26:38.061
Pretty soon

00:26:38.129 --> 00:26:40.791
even Admiral Maclntyre
stopped returning my calls.

00:26:40.865 --> 00:26:44.164
So I resigned from Starfleet.

00:26:47.072 --> 00:26:49.131
For the record,

00:26:49.207 --> 00:26:55.339
Seven's translink
frequency is 108.44236000.

00:26:56.414 --> 00:26:58.211
Could be our lucky number.

00:26:58.283 --> 00:27:00.274
I'm encoding it now.

00:27:00.352 --> 00:27:04.288
When did you embark
on your life of crime?

00:27:07.058 --> 00:27:10.391
The second I heard
about this little gem.

00:27:11.463 --> 00:27:13.328
Mr. Kim, did you ever stop

00:27:13.398 --> 00:27:16.231
to think about what you're
trying to do here?

00:27:16.301 --> 00:27:19.099
Altering the timeline
may make things worse.

00:27:19.170 --> 00:27:21.070
At least
you and Chakotay survived.

00:27:21.139 --> 00:27:22.401
Why tempt fate?

00:27:22.474 --> 00:27:24.408
This "timeline" only exists

00:27:24.476 --> 00:27:26.774
because I made a mistake
15 years ago.

00:27:26.845 --> 00:27:29.609
The crew trusted in me
and I let them down.

00:27:30.649 --> 00:27:32.082
Tactical alert.

00:27:32.150 --> 00:27:36.177
Vessel approaching,
bearing 184 mark 7.

00:27:43.695 --> 00:27:44.753
They've found us.

00:27:44.829 --> 00:27:46.194
Chakotay.

00:27:46.264 --> 00:27:47.390
Go ahead.

00:27:47.465 --> 00:27:49.524
Starfleet's
on an intercept course.

00:27:49.601 --> 00:27:51.034
It's now or never.

00:27:51.102 --> 00:27:52.569
We're on our way.

00:27:55.373 --> 00:27:57.933
If you're having doubts,
let me know.

00:27:58.076 --> 00:28:00.135
I'll take your program off-line.

00:28:01.513 --> 00:28:05.677
But if you're with us,
we tempt fate together.

00:28:08.019 --> 00:28:10.385
To aid an honorable thief

00:28:10.455 --> 00:28:14.653
or to spend eternity
in cybernetic oblivion?

00:28:14.726 --> 00:28:17.752
Let's tempt fate.

00:28:28.707 --> 00:28:32.734
Captain's Log, Stardate 52143.6.

00:28:32.811 --> 00:28:34.870
With any luck, my next log entry

00:28:34.946 --> 00:28:36.914
will be made
in the Alpha Quadrant,

00:28:37.048 --> 00:28:40.108
but should our luck run out,
I'd like to say for the record

00:28:40.185 --> 00:28:43.416
that the crew of Voyager acted
with distinction and valor.

00:28:43.488 --> 00:28:44.819
Shield generators?

00:28:44.889 --> 00:28:46.413
On line.

00:28:46.491 --> 00:28:47.753
Plasma flow?

00:28:47.826 --> 00:28:49.054
Stable.

00:28:49.127 --> 00:28:50.094
Com-link?

00:28:50.161 --> 00:28:51.651
Secure.

00:28:51.730 --> 00:28:52.424
Lunch?

00:28:53.665 --> 00:28:55.098
Salami sandwiches.

00:28:56.434 --> 00:28:58.061
Feel up to this, Ensign?

00:28:58.136 --> 00:28:59.763
Yes, sir.

00:28:59.838 --> 00:29:01.806
Chakotay to Voyager.

00:29:01.873 --> 00:29:02.862
We're ready.

00:29:02.941 --> 00:29:05.705
All hands, this is the Captain.

00:29:05.777 --> 00:29:08.245
Take your stations,

00:29:08.313 --> 00:29:11.305
secure all systems,

00:29:11.382 --> 00:29:14.317
and stand by
for the jump to slipstream.

00:29:19.090 --> 00:29:21.388
I've established a telemetry
link with the shuttle.

00:29:21.459 --> 00:29:23.256
Match their course and speed.

00:29:30.335 --> 00:29:31.597
They're gaining on us.

00:29:31.669 --> 00:29:33.432
200,000 kilometers and closing.

00:29:33.505 --> 00:29:35.496
You call these
evasive maneuvers?

00:29:35.573 --> 00:29:37.438
I'm doing my best.

00:29:37.509 --> 00:29:39.101
Harry, status?

00:29:39.177 --> 00:29:41.407
The Borg transmitter's on line,
but I'm still waiting

00:29:41.479 --> 00:29:43.640
for the Doctor to give me
the temporal coordinates.

00:29:43.715 --> 00:29:45.012
Just a few more minutes.

00:29:45.083 --> 00:29:46.015
Speed it up.

00:29:46.084 --> 00:29:47.711
We've got a Galaxy-class
starship on our tail.

00:29:47.786 --> 00:29:49.253
I'm working as fast as I can.

00:29:49.320 --> 00:29:50.912
They're hailing us.

00:29:50.989 --> 00:29:52.616
You want to talk to them?

00:29:52.690 --> 00:29:55.124
It could buy us some time.

00:29:55.193 --> 00:29:57.093
Open a channel.

00:29:57.162 --> 00:30:00.359
This is Captain La Forge
of the Starship Challenger.

00:30:00.431 --> 00:30:02.126
You seem to be in quite a hurry.

00:30:02.200 --> 00:30:03.360
You could say that.

00:30:03.434 --> 00:30:04.833
Why don't you

00:30:04.903 --> 00:30:07.201
shut down those impulse engines,
drop your shields

00:30:07.272 --> 00:30:09.069
and let's talk about this
face-to-face?

00:30:09.140 --> 00:30:10.767
Mind if I take a rain check?

00:30:10.842 --> 00:30:12.571
As a matter of fact, I do.

00:30:12.644 --> 00:30:14.475
We know what you're
about to attempt

00:30:14.546 --> 00:30:15.945
and we can't let that happen,

00:30:16.047 --> 00:30:19.073
so the Federation Council is
willing to make you an offer...

00:30:19.150 --> 00:30:22.210
hand over the Borg transmitter,
stand down your vessel

00:30:22.287 --> 00:30:24.778
and the charges of conspiracy
will be dropped.

00:30:24.856 --> 00:30:26.289
That's not much of an offer.

00:30:26.357 --> 00:30:27.824
If we succeed, those charges

00:30:27.892 --> 00:30:29.917
will never have existed
in the first place.

00:30:29.994 --> 00:30:32.929
If you succeed, countless lives
will be affected.

00:30:32.997 --> 00:30:36.524
We're here to save 150 lives...
our crew.

00:30:36.601 --> 00:30:37.966
I understand and I might

00:30:38.036 --> 00:30:40.937
be doing the same thing
if I were in your position,

00:30:41.005 --> 00:30:42.973
but I've got my own crew
to protect,

00:30:43.041 --> 00:30:44.975
not to mention
15 years of history,

00:30:45.043 --> 00:30:48.877
so... I'm asking you again.

00:30:48.947 --> 00:30:52.280
Stand down
and return the transmitter.

00:30:52.350 --> 00:30:54.511
You know I can't do that.

00:30:54.586 --> 00:30:56.645
And you know
I have to try to stop you.

00:30:56.721 --> 00:30:58.484
Yes, I know.

00:30:58.556 --> 00:30:59.989
Good luck.

00:31:00.091 --> 00:31:02.116
Same to you.

00:31:06.397 --> 00:31:08.228
They're targeting our engines.

00:31:08.299 --> 00:31:09.698
Shields to full.

00:31:09.767 --> 00:31:11.325
Stand by weapons.

00:31:17.408 --> 00:31:18.841
Voyager to Chakotay.

00:31:18.910 --> 00:31:20.070
Yes, ma'am.

00:31:20.144 --> 00:31:22.112
Prepare to enter the slipstream.

00:31:22.180 --> 00:31:24.307
Acknowledged.

00:31:24.382 --> 00:31:26.043
Engage.

00:31:28.052 --> 00:31:34.287
Slipstream velocity
in four, three, two...

00:31:41.332 --> 00:31:43.163
Shields down to 62 percent.

00:31:43.234 --> 00:31:45.896
Return fire.

00:31:45.970 --> 00:31:48.370
Direct hit.
No effect on their shields.

00:31:48.439 --> 00:31:50.532
We're no match for them,
Chakotay.

00:31:50.608 --> 00:31:51.666
Keep trying.

00:31:53.912 --> 00:31:55.140
I don't mean to be a pest,

00:31:55.213 --> 00:31:56.908
but we're losing power
back here.

00:31:56.981 --> 00:31:58.778
Hold on. We're switching
to emergency backup.

00:32:00.618 --> 00:32:01.915
Thank you.

00:32:02.053 --> 00:32:05.386
Doc, I need those
temporal coordinates now.

00:32:05.456 --> 00:32:07.253
Badgering me won't help.

00:32:08.993 --> 00:32:10.893
I'm detecting a phase variance...

00:32:10.962 --> 00:32:14.295
point one, point two...

00:32:14.365 --> 00:32:15.127
Helm?

00:32:15.199 --> 00:32:16.723
I'm still waiting for Harry.

00:32:16.801 --> 00:32:17.927
Point three.

00:32:18.002 --> 00:32:18.934
Voyager to Delta Flyer.

00:32:19.003 --> 00:32:20.800
We need those corrections

00:32:20.872 --> 00:32:22.669
or we'll have
to shut down the drive.

00:32:22.740 --> 00:32:23.934
We're on it, Captain.

00:32:25.877 --> 00:32:27.936
The threshold is fluctuating.

00:32:28.012 --> 00:32:31.413
Okay. I can do this.

00:32:31.482 --> 00:32:35.612
I'm compensating
for the spatial gradients...

00:32:35.687 --> 00:32:39.179
Deflector geometry stable.

00:32:40.992 --> 00:32:42.755
Got it!

00:32:44.195 --> 00:32:46.595
I'm receiving
the phase corrections.

00:32:46.664 --> 00:32:48.928
The phase variance
is decreasing.

00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:50.433
Shields are holding.

00:32:50.501 --> 00:32:53.299
Looks like we're on our way.

00:32:53.371 --> 00:32:55.965
Phase variance is increasing.

00:32:56.107 --> 00:32:59.167
Point three... point four.

00:32:59.243 --> 00:33:00.471
Harry, what's happening?

00:33:00.545 --> 00:33:03.275
The phase variance
is still increasing.

00:33:03.348 --> 00:33:04.906
I-I'm not sure, Captain.

00:33:04.983 --> 00:33:06.382
It should be working.

00:33:06.451 --> 00:33:07.577
I need an answer, Harry.

00:33:07.652 --> 00:33:08.983
We're running out of time.

00:33:10.888 --> 00:33:13.288
Let me try
recalibrating the sensors.

00:33:13.358 --> 00:33:15.952
I might be overcompensating
for the variance in the...

00:33:18.997 --> 00:33:20.362
We've lost our com-link.

00:33:20.431 --> 00:33:22.695
Telemetry's down, too.

00:33:22.767 --> 00:33:24.792
The slipstream's destabilizing.

00:33:24.869 --> 00:33:26.302
Shut down the drive!

00:33:26.371 --> 00:33:27.633
I can't.

00:33:27.705 --> 00:33:29.935
There's some kind of overload
in the quantum matrix.

00:33:30.041 --> 00:33:31.133
I've lost helm control.

00:33:32.210 --> 00:33:33.643
I have it.

00:33:33.711 --> 00:33:35.372
Her cybernetic systems
were terminated

00:33:35.446 --> 00:33:38.108
on Stardate 52164.3,

00:33:38.182 --> 00:33:41.515
Borg time index 9.43852.

00:33:44.422 --> 00:33:47.414
You're encoding the transmitter
for time index 9.40?

00:33:47.492 --> 00:33:48.789
Uh-huh.

00:33:48.860 --> 00:33:50.828
That's less than four minutes
before Voyager was destroyed.

00:33:50.895 --> 00:33:52.453
Cutting it a little close,
aren't we?

00:33:52.530 --> 00:33:54.464
This is no ordinary
phone call, Doc.

00:33:54.532 --> 00:33:55.760
We're talking to yesterday.

00:33:55.833 --> 00:33:56.925
Timing is everything.

00:33:57.001 --> 00:33:59.333
I want to make sure Seven
of Nine gets the information

00:33:59.404 --> 00:34:00.564
at just the right moment.

00:34:02.106 --> 00:34:03.539
There.

00:34:06.277 --> 00:34:08.973
I'm bringing up
the new phase corrections.

00:34:11.382 --> 00:34:14.180
This was where I failed
15 years ago, Doc.

00:34:14.252 --> 00:34:16.686
This time will be different.

00:34:23.861 --> 00:34:25.829
Captain, I am receiving
a transmission.

00:34:25.897 --> 00:34:27.524
You said the com-link was down.

00:34:27.598 --> 00:34:28.724
It is.

00:34:28.800 --> 00:34:30.131
The signal is being routed

00:34:30.201 --> 00:34:31.930
through one
of my cranial implants.

00:34:32.036 --> 00:34:35.028
It contains
a new set of phase corrections.

00:34:35.106 --> 00:34:37.267
Does Harry know how to access
your Borg systems?

00:34:37.341 --> 00:34:38.569
No.

00:34:38.643 --> 00:34:40.338
He must have figured out a way.

00:34:40.411 --> 00:34:41.673
Enter the corrections.

00:34:43.714 --> 00:34:46.478
They're not compensating
for the phase variance.

00:34:46.551 --> 00:34:48.246
The slipstream is collapsing.

00:34:48.319 --> 00:34:49.786
Full power to the deflector.

00:34:49.854 --> 00:34:51.549
No effect.

00:34:51.622 --> 00:34:54.090
Our hull is buckling.

00:34:54.158 --> 00:34:55.887
Shields at maximum.
Hold her steady, Tom.

00:34:55.960 --> 00:34:58.087
It's no use.
We're losing attitude control.

00:34:59.197 --> 00:35:02.291
Inertial dampers off-line!

00:35:02.366 --> 00:35:03.458
What about the Delta Flyer?

00:35:03.534 --> 00:35:04.796
There is no sign of them.

00:35:04.869 --> 00:35:06.700
They must have remained
in the slipstream.

00:35:08.106 --> 00:35:10.700
Voyager's been thrown
into normal space.

00:35:10.775 --> 00:35:12.140
Alter our slipstream course.

00:35:12.210 --> 00:35:13.472
We've got to go back.

00:35:13.544 --> 00:35:14.806
We can't.

00:35:14.879 --> 00:35:17.848
Even if they survived reentry
at this velocity, we wouldn't.

00:35:17.915 --> 00:35:19.906
What are you saying?
We've got to find them!

00:35:20.051 --> 00:35:21.985
Ensign, there's no choice.

00:35:33.197 --> 00:35:36.792
Captain, we're just a few
parsecs from the Alpha Quadrant.

00:35:36.868 --> 00:35:39.393
Not exactly how I wanted
to cross the finish line.

00:35:39.470 --> 00:35:41.700
Hull breach
on Decks 5 through 10.

00:35:41.772 --> 00:35:43.399
We're losing life support.

00:35:44.809 --> 00:35:45.935
If we don't land the ship,

00:35:46.077 --> 00:35:47.738
we're risking
structural collapse.

00:35:49.247 --> 00:35:52.842
I'm reading a planet
nine million kilometers ahead.

00:35:52.917 --> 00:35:55.477
It's Class-L.

00:35:55.553 --> 00:35:56.315
Do it.

00:36:01.392 --> 00:36:03.883
We're coming in too fast.
Reverse thrusters.

00:36:04.028 --> 00:36:07.191
All hands, brace for impact!

00:36:31.822 --> 00:36:33.084
We're still here.

00:36:33.157 --> 00:36:34.852
Why are we still here?

00:36:34.926 --> 00:36:35.984
Mr. Kim?

00:36:37.562 --> 00:36:39.257
The new phase corrections
didn't work.

00:36:39.330 --> 00:36:40.695
Are you certain?

00:36:40.765 --> 00:36:42.756
If Voyager had gotten
through safely,

00:36:42.833 --> 00:36:45.495
we wouldn't still be here
trying to save them.

00:36:45.570 --> 00:36:47.094
The transmitter's functioning.

00:36:47.171 --> 00:36:49.662
Seven must have received
our message.

00:36:49.740 --> 00:36:51.674
Chakotay, problems!

00:36:51.742 --> 00:36:52.709
I can see that.

00:36:54.845 --> 00:36:55.834
Our engines are down.

00:36:55.913 --> 00:36:58.177
They're locking on to us
with a tractor beam.

00:36:58.249 --> 00:36:59.409
Full thrusters.

00:37:00.751 --> 00:37:02.048
No effect.

00:37:04.422 --> 00:37:06.617
Do we have enough power
to send a plasma surge

00:37:06.691 --> 00:37:09.251
through their tractor beam;
break ourselves free?

00:37:09.327 --> 00:37:10.555
I think so,

00:37:10.628 --> 00:37:12.755
but the EPS relays
have taken heavy damage.

00:37:12.830 --> 00:37:14.991
It could destabilize
the warp core.

00:37:15.066 --> 00:37:17.000
If you want to beam
over to that ship,

00:37:17.068 --> 00:37:18.194
I'll understand.

00:37:18.269 --> 00:37:20.863
And let you have all the fun?

00:37:23.374 --> 00:37:26.810
Harry, we just bought you
a few more minutes.

00:37:26.877 --> 00:37:27.901
Acknowledged.

00:37:28.045 --> 00:37:29.444
I'm no time travel expert,

00:37:29.513 --> 00:37:31.572
but can't we just
call Voyager again?

00:37:31.649 --> 00:37:33.344
The past isn't going anywhere.

00:37:33.417 --> 00:37:34.543
That's not going to help

00:37:34.619 --> 00:37:36.416
if we don't know
what to tell them.

00:37:42.059 --> 00:37:44.186
The slipstream
kinetics look right.

00:37:44.262 --> 00:37:47.129
Hyperdimensional
progressions... perfect.

00:37:48.599 --> 00:37:51.329
Maybe it's
the deflector geometry.

00:37:57.642 --> 00:37:58.666
We're free.

00:37:58.743 --> 00:38:00.643
The EPS relays are overloading.

00:38:00.711 --> 00:38:03.509
Harry, we're looking
at a possible core breach

00:38:03.581 --> 00:38:05.242
in less than three minutes.

00:38:05.316 --> 00:38:07.375
How's it coming back there?

00:38:07.451 --> 00:38:09.612
Great! Just great!

00:38:09.687 --> 00:38:11.985
It took me ten years
to make these corrections.

00:38:12.056 --> 00:38:13.455
I can't fix it in three minutes!

00:38:13.524 --> 00:38:14.684
You've got to try!

00:38:14.759 --> 00:38:17.819
I can't!
It's not working.

00:38:17.895 --> 00:38:19.385
Why won't it work?!

00:38:21.799 --> 00:38:22.891
I killed them!

00:38:22.967 --> 00:38:24.059
Control yourself.

00:38:24.135 --> 00:38:25.659
They trusted me,
and I killed them!

00:38:25.736 --> 00:38:28.330
Mr. Kim! I didn't spend all
those years in an ice bucket,

00:38:28.406 --> 00:38:30.306
so I could listen
to you berate yourself.

00:38:30.374 --> 00:38:32.308
If you want to wallow
in self-pity, fine!

00:38:32.376 --> 00:38:33.638
Do it on your own time!

00:38:33.711 --> 00:38:36.373
Don't you see?
History's repeating itself.

00:38:36.447 --> 00:38:39.575
I destroyed Voyager once,
and I'm doing it again!

00:38:39.650 --> 00:38:42.813
Somebody has got to knuckle
down and change history

00:38:42.887 --> 00:38:44.377
and that somebody is you.

00:38:44.455 --> 00:38:46.923
It can't be done, Doc.
I told you.

00:38:47.058 --> 00:38:50.289
No, you told me, you can't
correct their phase variance.

00:38:50.361 --> 00:38:52.056
All right.
We have to accept that.

00:38:52.129 --> 00:38:54.222
But what about
sending Voyager a warning?

00:38:54.298 --> 00:38:57.734
Is there a way to get them
to abort the slipstream flight?

00:38:57.802 --> 00:39:00.066
Yes. Yes!

00:39:00.137 --> 00:39:01.570
I could send a phase correction

00:39:01.639 --> 00:39:03.607
which would disperse
the slipstream entirely.

00:39:03.674 --> 00:39:04.868
If we can't get the crew home,

00:39:04.942 --> 00:39:06.239
at least
we can save their lives!

00:39:06.310 --> 00:39:09.404
Warning. Warp core breach
in 60 seconds.

00:39:09.480 --> 00:39:11.414
Can you eject the core?

00:39:11.482 --> 00:39:12.574
No.

00:39:12.650 --> 00:39:13.981
Emergency systems are off-line.

00:39:14.051 --> 00:39:15.609
La Forge to Delta Flyer.

00:39:15.686 --> 00:39:18.746
Our sensors are reading
an overload in your warp matrix.

00:39:18.823 --> 00:39:20.085
Lower your shields.

00:39:20.157 --> 00:39:21.647
We'll beam you out of there.

00:39:21.726 --> 00:39:25.890
I appreciate the offer, Captain,
but the answer's no.

00:39:26.030 --> 00:39:28.089
I suggest you get
to a safe distance.

00:39:28.165 --> 00:39:32.499
Warning. Warp core breach
in 45 seconds.

00:39:32.570 --> 00:39:35.300
Harry, now would be a good time.

00:39:36.907 --> 00:39:39.569
Mr. Kim!

00:39:39.643 --> 00:39:41.110
It's losing power.

00:39:42.813 --> 00:39:45.407
Warning. Warp core breach
in 30 seconds.

00:39:45.483 --> 00:39:46.415
Your emitter.

00:39:46.484 --> 00:39:47.576
It's got its own power source.

00:39:47.651 --> 00:39:48.583
Would it be enough?

00:39:48.652 --> 00:39:50.449
It's our only chance.

00:39:51.555 --> 00:39:52.920
Glad you could join us, Doc.

00:39:52.990 --> 00:39:54.116
It's been a pleasure.

00:39:56.494 --> 00:39:59.861
Warning. Warp core breach
in 15 seconds.

00:40:01.399 --> 00:40:03.924
Chakotay,
I'm giving this one more try.

00:40:04.068 --> 00:40:10.337
Warning. Warp core breach
in ten, nine, eight, seven, six,

00:40:10.408 --> 00:40:14.469
five, four, three, two, one...

00:40:14.545 --> 00:40:15.739
Yes!

00:40:22.019 --> 00:40:24.112
Captain, I am receiving
a transmission.

00:40:24.188 --> 00:40:25.815
I thought you said
the com-link was down.

00:40:25.890 --> 00:40:27.050
It is.

00:40:27.124 --> 00:40:28.716
The signal is being routed

00:40:28.793 --> 00:40:30.761
through one
of my cranial implants.

00:40:30.828 --> 00:40:33.319
It contains
a new set of phase corrections.

00:40:33.397 --> 00:40:35.558
Does Harry know how to access
your Borg systems?

00:40:35.633 --> 00:40:36.793
No.

00:40:36.867 --> 00:40:38.494
He must have figured out a way.

00:40:38.569 --> 00:40:39.968
Enter the corrections.

00:40:43.474 --> 00:40:46.136
Captain, the quantum drive
just went off-line.

00:40:46.210 --> 00:40:47.837
We're dropping to impulse.

00:40:47.912 --> 00:40:50.574
Captain,
we've lost the slipstream.

00:40:57.655 --> 00:40:59.316
The slipstream collapsed.

00:40:59.390 --> 00:41:01.915
We were thrown out right along
with Voyager.

00:41:02.059 --> 00:41:03.026
Our com system's back up.

00:41:03.093 --> 00:41:04.025
Delta Flyer to Voyager.

00:41:04.094 --> 00:41:05.186
What happened?

00:41:05.262 --> 00:41:07.696
You miscalculated, Harry.

00:41:07.765 --> 00:41:09.494
We entered
the exact phase corrections

00:41:09.567 --> 00:41:10.795
you sent to Seven of Nine.

00:41:10.868 --> 00:41:13.598
They shut down
the quantum drive.

00:41:13.671 --> 00:41:15.104
Captain,

00:41:15.172 --> 00:41:17.970
I didn't send any corrections
to Seven of Nine.

00:41:19.443 --> 00:41:20.933
She received a message

00:41:21.045 --> 00:41:23.536
through one
of her cranial implants.

00:41:23.614 --> 00:41:24.876
It wasn't you?

00:41:24.949 --> 00:41:26.109
No, ma'am.

00:41:31.622 --> 00:41:33.681
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:41:33.757 --> 00:41:36.351
Our slipstream flight
may have been brief,

00:41:36.427 --> 00:41:39.225
but it took nearly ten years
off our journey.

00:41:39.296 --> 00:41:42.356
I've given the order
to dismantle the quantum drive

00:41:42.433 --> 00:41:44.958
until the technology
can be perfected.

00:41:45.035 --> 00:41:48.971
Despite the setback, we have
a renewed sense of momentum.

00:41:49.039 --> 00:41:53.169
It no longer seems a question
of if we get home, but when.

00:42:02.419 --> 00:42:03.613
At ease.

00:42:05.523 --> 00:42:07.252
Am I interrupting?

00:42:07.324 --> 00:42:08.916
No.

00:42:08.993 --> 00:42:11.461
I just came here to try
to figure things out.

00:42:11.529 --> 00:42:13.520
Phase corrections.

00:42:13.597 --> 00:42:16.657
The corrections
I sent you were wrong.

00:42:16.734 --> 00:42:17.792
If you had used them,

00:42:17.868 --> 00:42:19.927
Voyager would have been
heavily damaged,

00:42:20.004 --> 00:42:22.063
maybe even destroyed.

00:42:22.139 --> 00:42:23.299
What I can't figure out

00:42:23.374 --> 00:42:26.537
is who sent the other phase
corrections to Seven of Nine.

00:42:26.610 --> 00:42:29.374
Looks like we've got
a guardian angel.

00:42:29.446 --> 00:42:31.380
Oh, I wish I could believe that.

00:42:31.448 --> 00:42:32.710
Believe it.

00:42:32.783 --> 00:42:34.876
His name is Harry Kim.

00:42:34.952 --> 00:42:36.510
Captain?

00:42:37.855 --> 00:42:40.881
Seven found a Starfleet
security code

00:42:40.958 --> 00:42:43.426
embedded in the transmission...

00:42:43.494 --> 00:42:45.359
yours.

00:42:45.429 --> 00:42:47.897
I'm telling you,
I didn't send it.

00:42:47.965 --> 00:42:49.956
Not yet.

00:42:50.100 --> 00:42:53.126
The transmission had
a temporal displacement.

00:42:53.203 --> 00:42:56.434
We believe it originated
from the future...

00:42:56.507 --> 00:42:58.634
ten, 20 years from now.

00:42:58.709 --> 00:43:00.540
We can't be sure.

00:43:03.147 --> 00:43:05.342
Wait a second.

00:43:05.416 --> 00:43:08.146
If I sent a message
from the future

00:43:08.218 --> 00:43:10.482
and changed the past,

00:43:10.554 --> 00:43:15.457
then that future would
no longer exist, right?

00:43:15.526 --> 00:43:17.858
So... how could I
have sent the message

00:43:17.928 --> 00:43:19.361
in the first place?

00:43:19.430 --> 00:43:20.920
Am I making any sense?

00:43:21.065 --> 00:43:22.657
My advice in making sense

00:43:22.733 --> 00:43:24.860
of temporal paradoxes
is simple...

00:43:24.935 --> 00:43:27.199
don't even try.

00:43:27.271 --> 00:43:30.365
To me...

00:43:30.441 --> 00:43:33.274
all that matters
is that somewhere

00:43:33.344 --> 00:43:37.610
somehow... sometime,

00:43:37.681 --> 00:43:41.617
you'll come through for us.

00:43:41.685 --> 00:43:44.745
Well, if you won't
take it from me,

00:43:44.822 --> 00:43:46.483
take it from you.

00:43:49.893 --> 00:43:54.296
Seven found a log entry
encoded in the telemetry...

00:43:54.365 --> 00:43:58.199
from Harry Kim

00:43:58.268 --> 00:44:00.736
to Harry Kim.

00:44:27.731 --> 00:44:29.289
Hello, Harry.

00:44:29.366 --> 00:44:33.234
I don't have much time
so listen to me.

00:44:33.303 --> 00:44:39.139
15 years ago, I made a mistake
and 150 people died.

00:44:39.209 --> 00:44:43.168
I've spent every day since then
regretting that mistake,

00:44:43.247 --> 00:44:45.374
but if you're watching
this right now,

00:44:45.449 --> 00:44:48.509
that means
all of that's changed.

00:44:48.585 --> 00:44:50.382
You owe me one.

00:44:50.454 --> 00:44:54.117
Mr. Kim, your assistance,
please.

00:44:54.191 --> 00:44:56.022
Got to go.
